<SiteChrome title="Privacy & cookies | Eurofizzion" description="What Eurofizzion collects (very little), the optional Google Analytics cookies, and YouTube videos." canonical="/privacy/">
  <section class="wrap entries-section prose" style="padding-top:64px">
    <div class="kicker">The small print</div>
    <h1 class="h2">Privacy &amp; cookies</h1>
    <p class="lede">Eurofizzion is an unofficial fan site. There are no accounts, no forms and no ads.</p>

    <h2>Who runs Eurofizzion</h2>
    <p>
      Eurofizzion is an idea by Jan Jaap Nijemeisland and is managed under RO Brand, KvK (Dutch Chamber of Commerce) number 58083111, Fokkerstraat 12,
      3833 LD Leusden, the Netherlands.
    </p>
    <p>Questions about privacy, or anything else: <a href="mailto:sing@eurofizzion.com">sing@eurofizzion.com</a>.</p>

    <h2>Analytics, only if you accept</h2>
    <p>
      If you click <b>Accept</b> in the cookie bar, we use Google Analytics (Google Ireland Ltd.) to count visits and see which pages people like. It sets
      cookies (<code>_ga</code>, <code>_ga_*</code>) and sends Google which pages you view, your browser and device type, and your approximate location.
      Google Analytics doesn’t log or store IP addresses. We don’t use it for advertising, and ad cookies stay switched off.
    </p>
    <p>If you click <b>Decline</b>, or don’t choose at all, Google Analytics isn’t loaded and nothing is sent to Google for analytics.</p>
    <p>You can change your mind at any time: <a href="#cookies" data-consent-open>open the cookie settings</a>. Declining after accepting removes the analytics cookies.</p>

    <h2>Your choice</h2>
    <p>We remember your choice in your browser’s local storage (<code>ef-consent</code>), so the bar doesn’t ask again. It never leaves your device.</p>

    <h2>YouTube videos</h2>
    <p>
      Video thumbnails are loaded from YouTube (<code>i.ytimg.com</code>). A video player only loads when you press play. It uses
      <code>youtube-nocookie.com</code>, YouTube’s privacy-enhanced mode, and Google’s own privacy policy applies to it.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>The site is hosted on Netlify, which processes standard server logs (such as IP addresses) to deliver and protect the site.</p>
  </section>
</SiteChrome>
